    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d195-a1">

                <pb facs="0315" n="235" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg235"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Prince Chi’ng</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-05-26"><hi rendition="#italic">May 26,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">F. O., No. 387.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Highness</hi>: I have the honor to inform Your
                    Highness that, at the request of the President of the Cuban Republic, my
                    Government has instructed me to respectfully ask the Chinese Government if it
                    will not permit the United States consular officers in China to use their good
                    offices in the representation of the interests of Cuba and her citizens until
                    such time as Cuban consuls shall have been appointed to reside in the
                    Empire.</p>
                <p>Trusting that I may have the early pleasure of informing my Government that the
                    requested permission is granted, I improve the occasion to reassure Your
                    Highness, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. H. Conger.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
